FUNCTION INTEGER GETDRIVE()

      Params:
  Return Val: Drive number for current drive


    Comments: Drive numbers correspond to drive letters in the following way
              A: = 0
              B: = 1
              C: = 2
              etc...


     Example: drive = GETDRIVE()
              if (drive == 2) println "Current drive is 'C'"



   See Also:  MKDIR, RMDIR, CWD



----------------------------------------------------------------------------


STATEMENT MKDIR STRING path

      Params: path = DOS path string for directory to create.
  Return Val: NA


    Comments: This statement can be used to create a DOS directory.


     Example: MKDIR "\PPE\TEST"



   See Also:  MKDIR, RMDIR, CWD


----------------------------------------------------------------------------


STATEMENT RMDIR STRING path

      Params: path = DOS path string for directory to remove.
  Return Val: NA


    Comments: This statement can be used to remove a DOS directory.
              The directory must be empty before removing it.


     Example: RMDIR "\PPE\TEST"



   See Also:  MKDIR, RMDIR, CWD


----------------------------------------------------------------------------


FUNCTION STRING CWD

      Params: NA
  Return Val: Reruns a string containing the Current Working Directory


    Comments: This statement can be used to determine the current DOS
              directory.


     Example: Println "Current working directory = ",CWD()



   See Also:  MKDIR, RMDIR, CWD

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------


STATEMENT ADJTUBYTES INTEGER bytes

      Params: bytes = number of bytes to adjust current users upload bytes with.
              This can be a positive or negative value
  Return Val: NA


    Comments: This statement can be used to adjust a users total uploads bytes
              up or down.


     Example: GETALTUSER 10
              ADJTUBYTES -2000
              PUTALTUSER




   See Also:  ADJ

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------



STATEMENT GRAFMODE INTEGER mode

      Params: mode = Graphics mode to switch to.
              1= If user has ANSI capabilities it will change graphics to color
                 ANSI
              2= Will attempt to put user in color ansi regardless of ansi ability
              3= Puts user in ansi-black and white mode
              4= Puts user in non-ansi black and white mode
              5= If user has RIP ability, will put user in RIP mode.
  Return Val: NA


    Comments: This statement can be used to change a users graphics mode while
              online.


     Example: PRINTLN "Changing to color ansi mode"
              GRAFMODE 1
              PRINTLN "Ohhh what a great example! "






   See Also:

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------



STATEMENT FDOQADD STRING addr, STRING file, INTEGER flags

      Params: addr = Fido address to send to
              file = filename to add to queue
              flags= queue flags for Crash Hold etc
              NORMAL = 1
              CRASH  = 2
              HOLD   = 3
  Return Val: NA


    Comments: This statement can be used to add entries to the FIDO queue.


     Example: FDOQADD "1/311/40","c:\pkts\094fc869.pkt",2








   See Also:

